cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CAD as Code: Parametric Modeling and Engineering with Python"
message: "If you use this book, please cite it as below."
type: book
authors:
  - given-names: David M.
    family-names: Straub
abstract: >-
  A book on parametric modeling and engineering with Python, covering
  boundary representations, the mathematics of curves and surfaces,
  freeform modeling, testable and release-ready models, meshing,
  simulation, and design-space search, using CadQuery and the OpenCascade
  kernel throughout.
keywords:
  - CAD
  - parametric modeling
  - computational geometry
  - CadQuery
  - OpenCascade
  - Python
  - engineering design
  - finite element method
